Maximum stats help for a lot more than just spell casting.  Try
convorting with a foocubus with low stats, and then try again
with them all maxed and see the difference.  Since a blessed
!ofGA increases them all across the board until any one hits
its maximum, targetting as many as possible as high as possible
is good strategy.  It isn't a do-it-or-die-guaranteed strategy,
but it's beneficial enough to try to bless every !oGA you
enoughter until most stats are near their maximum.

> Who says it's non-spellcasting?
> Almost any class can benefit to some degree from spells.

Some players chose to go without spellcasting.  A Harry Potter
squib wizard perhaps.  But being able to cast spells is an
advantage whether you actually cast any spells or not.
Identify even at 80% failure rate rules when you're holding
a bunch of interesting stuff from your stash.  If your
character isn't a spellcasting specialist it's not like you
need to save all of your mana for offensive spells ...

